    "body": "More follow-ups from the third review of PR #791 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/791#pullrequestreview-5855934812):\n- **The reverse of the inside-part crossing is only a warning:** cut L first, then E, gets only a KerfCrossing, because the judge checks later rings against earlier ones. When the later cut is Outer, it should also refuse an earlier ring that has a stretch strictly inside it and isn't enclosed by it. The generator refuses that layout today, but the law is the independent judge.\n- **The 2r cap on the corner tip zone refuses normal-sized inside V-notches sharper than about 30°** (e.g. a 20 mm mouth at 25° or 20°). That's the safe direction, but decision 4a should say it plainly.\n- **The vertex-touching diamond-hole case** in `a_ring_inside_an_earlier_part_touching_its_edge_is_refused` passes because the program is Malformed. It needs a fixture that actually reaches the laws.\n- **`Region::new` silently drops a zero-width slit** (predates #791): it may deserve its own issue.",
